MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Stabbing the Drama feels like a natural next choice because Figure Number Five already gives me a reason to explore more Soilwork, especially its mix of melody and heaviness.",
    "The End of Heartache and Ascendancy connect with the melodic riffs and aggressive vocals I enjoy in In Flames and Advance And Vanquish. Believe also gives me a clear follow-up to Ten Thousand Fists."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "St. Anger feels off because its raw, abrasive sound does not give me the melodic pull I want from heavy music right now.",
    "City of Evil and Vol. 3 appeal to me, but they feel less directly connected to my current interest in In Flames and Soilwork than my strongest picks do."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in heavy music seems to have been treated as enough to make different kinds of aggression equally appealing, even though melody matters a lot to my choices.",
    "An album being related to something I have heard makes it worth considering, but that alone does not mean I want to choose it today, as with The Sickness."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated listening to In Flames and my interest in Figure Number Five make the balance of melodic riffs and harsh vocals especially relevant to what I want now.",
    "I can find several albums appealing while only choosing a few. WAKING THE FALLEN and Shadows Are Security fit my interests, but I would save them while pursuing the stronger connections first."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understand my interest in heavy music, but my strongest choices depend on a particular balance of melody, aggression, and connections to albums I already know."
}
